# uv / virtualenvs
#
# No trailing slash on `.venv`. A trailing slash matches a *directory* only, and
# on this machine `.venv` is a reparse point onto `V:\dev\venvs\aggregate_api`,
# which git sees as a symlink rather than a directory. So `.venv/` did not match
# it, the link itself got committed as a 120000 blob holding the literal text
# `v:/dev/venvs/aggregate_api/`, and checking the repo out on Linux produced a
# dangling symlink to a path that cannot exist there. Untracked at a53.
#
# If you want the environment out of the repo directory, set
# `UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT` rather than making a link: it is per-machine, uv
# honors it directly, and there is nothing in the tree for git to pick up.
.venv
venv/

# pyenv
.python-version

